<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2016/Cell-Phone.jpg" alt="The cell phone waiting lot at Dulles Airport" width="550" height="395" data-filename="Cell Phone Waiting.JPG" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Cell Phone Waiting. 5x7, oil on linen panel.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">This was one of those little end-of-the-day sketches, the kind you do when the previous 5 hours in the studio haven't produced anything worthwhile. I based it on a photo I took at Dulles Airport one evening while waiting to pick up my wife.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The ground was painted with one or two strokes of thin paint - thereby sending 12 trucks, three cars, and the Fedex depot into oblivion. The result looks almost like a seascape.</p>
